IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `wills-dates`
IMPORT `wills-rules`
IMPORT `wills-seat-family`

-- Wills Act 1997 (Vic) -- worked cases for the family's and beneficiaries' questions (wills-seat-family.l4) and the s 31(2)
-- rule. Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text; none was copied from the encoding's output.
-- Each assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. The facts are illustrative.
-- Breached traces are asserted through the helper's CONSIDER ... WHEN FULFILLED (EVALTRACE ... EQUALS cannot test a breach).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `cases: the family and beneficiaries`

`d` MEANS `the calendar date`

§§ `s 3 -- domestic partner`

-- Arguments: registered relationship, married to the deceased, living as a couple on a genuine domestic basis.
#ASSERT `Was I the deceased's domestic partner` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Was I the deceased's domestic partner` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Was I the deceased's domestic partner` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Was I the deceased's domestic partner` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 50 -- who may see the will`

#ASSERT `Can I see the will` `a person named or referred to in the will` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I see the will` `a beneficiary named in an earlier will` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I see the will` `the deceased's spouse at the date of death` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I see the will` `the deceased's domestic partner` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I see the will` `a parent, guardian or child of the deceased` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I see the will` `a person entitled to a share if the deceased had died without a will` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I see the will` `a parent or guardian of a minor named in the will or entitled on intestacy` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I see the will` `a creditor or other claimant against the estate, with evidence of the claim` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I see the will` `a creditor or other claimant against the estate, without evidence of the claim` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can I see the will` `someone else` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 9 -- informal wills`

-- s 9(1). Arguments: what was not properly executed, Court satisfied of the intention.
#ASSERT `Can the Court accept the informal document as the will` `the whole document` TRUE EQUALS `the Court may admit it to probate as the will (s 9(1))`
#ASSERT `Can the Court accept the informal document as the will` `an alteration to the will` TRUE EQUALS `the Court may admit it to probate as the will (s 9(1))`
#ASSERT `Can the Court accept the informal document as the will` `the whole document` FALSE EQUALS `s 9 gives the Court no power on these facts: it is not satisfied the deceased intended it as their will`
#ASSERT `Can the Court accept the informal document as the will` `an alteration to the will` FALSE EQUALS `s 9 gives the Court no power on these facts: it is not satisfied the deceased intended it as their will`
#ASSERT `Can the Court accept the informal document as the will` `nothing: it was executed as the Act requires` TRUE EQUALS `no need: the document is executed as the Act requires`
#ASSERT `Can the Court accept the informal document as the will` `nothing: it was executed as the Act requires` FALSE EQUALS `no need: the document is executed as the Act requires`
-- s 9(2). Arguments: revoking writing executed, Court satisfied of the intention to revoke.
#ASSERT `Can the Court treat the will as revoked by the informal writing` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the Court treat the will as revoked by the informal writing` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the Court treat the will as revoked by the informal writing` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 9(5). Arguments: Registrar authorised, everyone consents, estate value, limit. "does not exceed": equal is within.
#ASSERT `Can the Registrar decide the informal will` TRUE TRUE 1000000 50000 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the Registrar decide the informal will` TRUE FALSE 50000 50000 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the Registrar decide the informal will` TRUE FALSE 49999 50000 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the Registrar decide the informal will` TRUE FALSE 50001 50000 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the Registrar decide the informal will` FALSE TRUE 1 50000 EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 31 -- rectification`

-- s 31(1). Arguments: reason, Court satisfied.
#ASSERT `Can the will be rectified` `a clerical error was made` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the will be rectified` `the will does not give effect to the will-maker's instructions` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the will be rectified` `a clerical error was made` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the will be rectified` `some other reason (a change of mind, a mistake about the law or the effect of the words)` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 31(2): the last day.
#ASSERT `By when must I apply for rectification` (`d` 10 1 2027) EQUALS `d` 10 7 2027
#ASSERT `By when must I apply for rectification` (`d` 31 8 2027) EQUALS `d` 29 2 2028
#ASSERT `By when must I apply for rectification` (`d` 31 3 2027) EQUALS `d` 30 9 2027
-- 10 January 2027 to 10 July 2027: 21 + 28 + 31 + 30 + 31 + 30 + 10 = 181 days.
#ASSERT `s 31(2) -- the days allowed to apply` (`d` 10 1 2027) EQUALS 181
-- The rule itself, through the helper: day 181 in time, day 182 late, day 0 in time.
#ASSERT `the application is in time under` (`s 31(2) -- apply for rectification within 6 months of the grant` (`d` 10 1 2027)) `at` 181
#ASSERT NOT (`the application is in time under` (`s 31(2) -- apply for rectification within 6 months of the grant` (`d` 10 1 2027)) `at` 182)
#ASSERT `the application is in time under` (`s 31(2) -- apply for rectification within 6 months of the grant` (`d` 10 1 2027)) `at` 0
-- s 31(2), (3). Arguments: granted, grant date, applied, date applied, today, Court extended, finally distributed.
#ASSERT `Is my rectification application in time` FALSE (`d` 1 1 2027) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2027) (`d` 1 6 2027) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no grant of probate yet: the six months have not begun`
#ASSERT `Is my rectification application in time` TRUE (`d` 10 1 2027) TRUE (`d` 10 7 2027) (`d` 1 8 2027) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `made in time (s 31(2))`
#ASSERT `Is my rectification application in time` TRUE (`d` 10 1 2027) TRUE (`d` 10 1 2027) (`d` 1 8 2027) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `made in time (s 31(2))`
#ASSERT `Is my rectification application in time` TRUE (`d` 10 1 2027) TRUE (`d` 1 2 2027) (`d` 1 8 2027) TRUE FALSE EQUALS `made in time (s 31(2))`
#ASSERT `Is my rectification application in time` TRUE (`d` 10 1 2027) TRUE (`d` 11 7 2027) (`d` 1 8 2027) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `out of time: I need the Court to extend the period (s 31(3))`
#ASSERT `Is my rectification application in time` TRUE (`d` 10 1 2027) TRUE (`d` 11 7 2027) (`d` 1 8 2027) TRUE FALSE EQUALS `out of time, but the Court has extended the period (s 31(3))`
#ASSERT `Is my rectification application in time` TRUE (`d` 10 1 2027) TRUE (`d` 11 7 2027) (`d` 1 8 2027) FALSE TRUE EQUALS `out of time, and the Court cannot extend it: the estate has been finally distributed (s 31(3))`
#ASSERT `Is my rectification application in time` TRUE (`d` 10 1 2027) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2027) (`d` 1 5 2027) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `still open: I can apply in time`
#ASSERT `Is my rectification application in time` TRUE (`d` 10 1 2027) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2027) (`d` 10 7 2027) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `still open: I can apply in time`
#ASSERT `Is my rectification application in time` TRUE (`d` 10 1 2027) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2027) (`d` 11 7 2027) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `out of time: I need the Court to extend the period (s 31(3))`
#ASSERT `Is my rectification application in time` TRUE (`d` 10 1 2027) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2027) (`d` 11 7 2027) FALSE TRUE EQUALS `out of time, and the Court cannot extend it: the estate has been finally distributed (s 31(3))`
-- Grant on 31 August 2027: last day 29 February 2028 (leap year).
#ASSERT `Is my rectification application in time` TRUE (`d` 31 8 2027) TRUE (`d` 29 2 2028) (`d` 1 4 2028) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `made in time (s 31(2))`
#ASSERT `Is my rectification application in time` TRUE (`d` 31 8 2027) TRUE (`d` 1 3 2028) (`d` 1 4 2028) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `out of time: I need the Court to extend the period (s 31(3))`

§§ `ss 39, 45 -- surviving by 30 days`

-- Arguments: will-maker's death, beneficiary's death. 1 March to 31 March 2027 is 30 days; to 1 April, 31.
#ASSERT `Did the beneficiary survive by 30 days` (`d` 1 3 2027) (`d` 31 3 2027) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Did the beneficiary survive by 30 days` (`d` 1 3 2027) (`d` 1 4 2027) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Did the beneficiary survive by 30 days` (`d` 1 3 2027) (`d` 1 3 2027) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Did the beneficiary survive by 30 days` (`d` 1 3 2027) (`d` 1 1 2027) EQUALS FALSE
-- Across 29 February 2028: 15 February to 16 March 2028 is 14 + 16 = 30 days; to 17 March, 31.
#ASSERT `Did the beneficiary survive by 30 days` (`d` 15 2 2028) (`d` 16 3 2028) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Did the beneficiary survive by 30 days` (`d` 15 2 2028) (`d` 17 3 2028) EQUALS TRUE

§§ `ss 35, 39, 45, 46(3) -- what becomes of the gift`

-- Arguments: beneficiary alive, will-maker's death, beneficiary's death, contrary intention, beneficiary was issue, their
-- issue survived by 30 days, class gift or interest ending at death, condition unmet, fractional share of residue.
#ASSERT `What becomes of the gift to the beneficiary who died` TRUE (`d` 1 3 2027) (`d` 1 3 2027) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the gift takes effect: the beneficiary survived the will-maker by 30 days`
#ASSERT `What becomes of the gift to the beneficiary who died` FALSE (`d` 1 3 2027) (`d` 1 4 2027) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the gift takes effect: the beneficiary survived the will-maker by 30 days`
#ASSERT `What becomes of the gift to the beneficiary who died` FALSE (`d` 1 3 2027) (`d` 31 3 2027) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the gift falls into the residuary estate (s 35(1))`
#ASSERT `What becomes of the gift to the beneficiary who died` FALSE (`d` 1 3 2027) (`d` 20 3 2027) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the will's own terms decide: it shows a contrary intention (ss 35(2), 39(2), 45(3))`
#ASSERT `What becomes of the gift to the beneficiary who died` FALSE (`d` 1 3 2027) (`d` 20 3 2027) FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the beneficiary's own issue who survive the will-maker by 30 days take the share (s 45(1))`
#ASSERT `What becomes of the gift to the beneficiary who died` FALSE (`d` 1 3 2027) (`d` 1 1 2027) FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the beneficiary's own issue who survive the will-maker by 30 days take the share (s 45(1))`
#ASSERT `What becomes of the gift to the beneficiary who died` FALSE (`d` 1 3 2027) (`d` 20 3 2027) FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the gift falls into the residuary estate (s 35(1))`
#ASSERT `What becomes of the gift to the beneficiary who died` FALSE (`d` 1 3 2027) (`d` 20 3 2027) FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the failed share passes to the other shares of the residue proportionately (s 46(3))`
#ASSERT `What becomes of the gift to the beneficiary who died` FALSE (`d` 1 3 2027) (`d` 20 3 2027) FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the gift falls into the residuary estate (s 35(1))`
#ASSERT `What becomes of the gift to the beneficiary who died` FALSE (`d` 1 3 2027) (`d` 1 1 2027) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the failed share passes to the other shares of the residue proportionately (s 46(3))`
#ASSERT `What becomes of the gift to the beneficiary who died` FALSE (`d` 1 3 2027) (`d` 1 1 2027) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the gift falls into the residuary estate (s 35(1))`

§§ `ss 21-25 -- a will for a relative who lacks capacity`

-- ss 21, 21B. Arguments: alive, lacks capacity, reflects likely intentions, reasonable.
#ASSERT `Can the Court authorise a will for my relative` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the Court authorise a will for my relative` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the Court authorise a will for my relative` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the Court authorise a will for my relative` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the Court authorise a will for my relative` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 21C.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to be heard on the statutory will application` `I am the person the will is for` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to be heard on the statutory will application` `I am the person's lawyer` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to be heard on the statutory will application` `I am the person's attorney under an enduring power of attorney` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to be heard on the statutory will application` `I am the person's guardian or administrator under the Guardianship and Administration Act 2019` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to be heard on the statutory will application` `the Court considers I have a genuine interest in the matter` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to be heard on the statutory will application` `none of these` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 25. Arguments: in writing, signed by the Registrar, sealed.
#ASSERT `Is the Court-authorised will valid` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the Court-authorised will valid` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is the Court-authorised will valid` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is the Court-authorised will valid` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
